id: no-effort
name: No Effort
type: instant
actionCost: 0
kiCost: 0
attacking: false
requiresTarget: false
usageLimit: 1/round
noEffort: true
# The effects it covers, `key=Label` each - asked which when it is used.
efforts: dynamic=Dynamic, sheathe=Un/Sheathing a Weapon, replace=Replace a Weapon, drop=Drop/Pickup, cancel-charge=Cancel Energy Charge, integrated=Activate/Deactivate Integrated Items
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Something that takes almost no time, once a Round on your turn: drawing or putting away a
  Weapon, dropping or picking something up, cancelling an Energy Charge, and the like.
text: >
  No Effort Maneuver [1/Round]: Anything incredibly easy to do, taking almost no time.
  –Maneuver Type: Instant
  –Action Cost: N/A
  –KP Cost: N/A
  –Effect: This Maneuver covers a lot of different effects which can only be used during your
  turn, which are listed below:

  * Dynamic. Anything that’s not covered here, your ARC may declare requires a No Effort
    Maneuver, such as attempting to talk to an Opponent for a length of time that exceeds
    typical combat banter but does not quite reach the level of a Combat Recovery.
  * Un/Sheathing a Weapon. Put away or draw a weapon.
  * Replace a Weapon. Replacing a Weapon you are holding with another Weapon you possess.
  * Drop/Pickup. Dropping or picking up an object.
  * Cancel Energy Charge. Stop suffering from the effects of the Energy Charge Maneuver, but
    you lose all gathered Energy Charges from your chosen Attacking Maneuver.
  * Activate/Deactivate Integrated Items. You may make an Active Integrated Item you possess
    become Inactive, and then choose one of your Inactive Integrated Items to become Active.

---

# --- What the system does ---------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Used: which effect, asked first - once a Round, during your turn, an Instant as any other.
# Cancel Energy Charge is done: the charge and its declaration go, as the Energy Cancel
# Maneuver's do, and it is offered only while there is one. The rest are said on the card.
#
# --- What the table keeps ----------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Dynamic - what the ARC declared - and Drop/Pickup: there are no objects here to drop.
#
# Activate/Deactivate Integrated Items: which to make Inactive and which Active, asked before
# anything is paid - also from the Gear tab's Activate/Deactivate (integrated.mjs).
